_(Activity display style)_:
: <select name="display">
  <?=mk_option($cfg['display'], "bar", _("Text with styled bar"))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['display'], "color", _("Text with color"))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['display'], "plain", _("Plain text"))?>
  </select>

> Choose how disk activity is shown in the Array/Pool device tables.
>
> **Text with styled bar** shows a color-coded progress bar with percentage overlay.
>
> **Text with color** shows the percentage number colored by activity level.
>
> **Plain text** shows just the percentage number with no styling.

_(Averaging window)_:
: <select name="window">
  <?=mk_option($cfg['window'], "2s", _("Instant (2s)"))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['window'], "10s", _("10 seconds"))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['window'], "1min", _("1 minute"))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['window'], "5min", _("5 minutes"))?>
  </select>

> How far back to average disk activity.
>
> **Instant** shows the raw 2-second sample (most responsive).
>
> **10 seconds / 1 minute / 5 minutes** smooth out spikes by averaging over that period.
>
> The column header updates to reflect the chosen window (e.g. "1MIN Activity").


### Disk wake attribution

_(Track HDD wake events)_:
: <select name="wake_tracking">
  <?=mk_option($cfg['wake_tracking'] ?? 'yes', "yes", _("Yes"))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['wake_tracking'] ?? 'yes', "no", _("No"))?>
  </select>

> When enabled, the plugin watches filesystem OPEN/ACCESS/MODIFY events with **fanotify** and correlates them with the rotational disk power state. A wake is recorded only when a physical device changes from STANDBY to ACTIVE.
>
> The history file is `/boot/config/plugins/disk.activity/wake-history.jsonl`. Only wake events are persisted; ordinary file-access events stay in RAM, avoiding continuous writes to the USB boot device.

_(Power-state source)_:
: <select name="wake_detector">
  <?=mk_option($cfg['wake_detector'] ?? 'auto', "auto", _("Auto: Unraid state, smartctl fallback (recommended)"))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['wake_detector'] ?? 'auto', "unraid", _("Unraid state only (zero disk probes)"))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['wake_detector'] ?? 'auto', "smartctl", _("smartctl -n standby only (physical verification)"))?>
  </select>

> **Auto** reads `/var/local/emhttp/disks.ini` first, which Unraid already refreshes, so the tracker normally does not send any extra command to the HDD. If Unraid does not expose a usable state, it falls back to `smartctl -n standby`. Use **smartctl only** when validating systems where the WebGUI spin state is known to be inaccurate.

_(Power-state polling interval)_:
: <select name="wake_poll">
  <?=mk_option($cfg['wake_poll'] ?? '10', "5", _("5 seconds"))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['wake_poll'] ?? '10', "10", _("10 seconds (recommended)"))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['wake_poll'] ?? '10', "15", _("15 seconds"))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['wake_poll'] ?? '10', "30", _("30 seconds"))?>
  </select>

> Shorter polling detects the STANDBY → ACTIVE transition sooner. In **Auto** mode, Unraid's cached state is used first; `smartctl -n standby` is only a fallback. The candidate process is timestamped at the actual filesystem event, not at the later power-state poll.

_(Verbose wake tracker log)_:
: <select name="wake_verbose">
  <?=mk_option($cfg['wake_verbose'] ?? 'no', "no", _("No"))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['wake_verbose'] ?? 'no', "yes", _("Yes"))?>
  </select>

> Debug output is written to `/var/log/disk_wake_monitor.log`. Leave this off for normal use.
>
> **Attribution limitations:** a HIGH result means the PID accessed the same mounted filesystem after the disk was confirmed asleep and before it was observed awake. If only a metadata syscall is involved, ZFS issues background I/O, or the access is hidden behind another filesystem layer, the event is deliberately shown as UNKNOWN instead of guessing.
>
> [Open Disk Wake History](/Settings/DiskWakeHistory)

